meta {
  name: 21. HIP data push (our dataPushUrl)
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{careUrl}}/api/abdm/v3/hiu/health-information/transfer
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{callbackToken}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "pageNumber": 1,
    "pageCount": 1,
    "transactionId": "{{transactionId}}",
    "entries": [
      {
        "content": "{{encryptedContent}}",
        "media": "application/fhir+json",
        "checksum": "{{contentChecksum}}",
        "careContextReference": "EPISODE-1"
      }
    ],
    "keyMaterial": {
      "cryptoAlg": "ECDH",
      "curve": "Curve25519",
      "dhPublicKey": {
        "expiry": "2026-12-31T00:00:00.000Z",
        "parameters": "Curve25519/32byte random key",
        "keyValue": "{{hipPublicKey}}"
      },
      "nonce": "{{hipNonce}}"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  The HIP posts here directly, not through the gateway (m2 .../05-m2-post-health-information-transfer).
  `dataPushUrl` = `${ABDM_CALLBACK_BASE_URL}/api/abdm/v3/hiu/health-information/transfer`.
  Operation id `m3-health-information-transfer`. The plug decrypts each entry with the key of the
  transaction (X25519 + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM), checks the MD5, stores the bundle, scrubs the
  ciphertext from the stored callback and notifies RECEIVED or FAILED.
  `encryptedContent`, `contentChecksum`, `hipPublicKey`, `hipNonce`: build them with
  `abdm.hip.crypto` against the `keyMaterial` the plug sent (see the smoke script).
}
